{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3324","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3324","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3324\",\"parent_revision\":\"8639b1dffc7d58b5a743cf88620217dadf19f3044c16a261f9e24724cfcc6de6\",\"root_revision\":\"8639b1dffc7d58b5a743cf88620217dadf19f3044c16a261f9e24724cfcc6de6\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nT6 (part of #3151's implementation) claimed to have \\\"demonstrated working end to end\\\" both the `PostToolUse` and `SubagentStop` hook dispatch paths through `skills/implementation-manager/scripts/task_status_hook.py`, citing 53 passing tests as evidence.\\n\\nThe orchestrator verified this claim and found it overstated: every one of those 53 tests calls the internal handler functions (`handle_subagent_stop`, `handle_activity_update`) directly, with the internal SAM-MCP subprocess call mocked. No test in the suite invokes `task_status_hook.py` itself as a real subprocess with hook-event JSON on stdin \u2014 the actual contract Claude Code uses to invoke it (per the script's own docstring: \\\"Receives JSON via stdin with hook context\\\").\\n\\nTraced `main()` (task_status_hook.py:961-988) and confirmed it's a thin dispatcher with no independent logic of its own \u2014 it parses stdin and calls exactly the two already-tested handler functions, and this entrypoint/`parse_hook_input()` were untouched by #3151's changes. So this is not a regression risk from that specific refactor, but it is a genuine, pre-existing test-coverage gap: nothing in the suite would catch a stdin-parsing or entrypoint-level regression in this hook script.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"40a52f578c6858430ca95791667f1b588d69f2a74cd939ee7e0c7f6f329ab59b\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRaDRtw\"}"}